                    "message": "Looks good other than"
                },
                {
                    "file": "tools/power-utils/aei_updater.cpp",
                    "line": 409,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Sorry, I should have noticed this before.  You should be casting to a `uint32*`, not an `int*`.\n\nC++ makes no promises on the size of an int.  It can be 2 bytes, 4 bytes, 8 bytes, depending on the target system processor.\n\nCasting to `uint32*` ensures 4 bytes.  Also, you want an unsigned value not a signed one.  int is signed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "tools/power-utils/aei_updater.cpp",
                    "line": 409,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Faisal Awada",
                        "email": "faisal@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "faisal-awada"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                }
